-- l4 batch over defaults that are EXPRESSIONS and are taken at a NAMED site
-- inside the rules (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md W7). Each default names a
-- section input, `alpha`, which the request supplies, so the value the site takes
-- is worked out from the request. Under hard each one is listed under the
-- application that took it, and only if the answer read it.

GIVETH A NUMBER
phi MEANS 8

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN alpha IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Config HAS
  timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi TIMES alpha)
  retries IS A NUMBER

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY (phi PLUS alpha)
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

@export default Combine
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      use IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS
  IF use
  THEN (scaled WITH base IS n) PLUS (Config WITH retries IS 1)'s timeout
  ELSE 0
